From 641b295381bf46c59f66017e0d55442058da3025 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: giteaguy <73799093+irnutsmurt@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 16:30:55 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 139/139] Save-data dialog: a full-screen picture, and it
 presents itself

The host's save-data dialog (cellSaveDataListLoad2/ListSave2, the new-save row,
the overwrite question) drawn as a full-screen picture in place of the text
panel: libs/video/osd_saves.c composes it on the CPU at the window's size (a
heading and a clock, the saves as rows with their ICON0.PNG, title, date, size
and DETAIL lines in mixed case, the selection, a scroll bar, the question, the
confirm and back prompts in a prompt style), with a font and prompt images the
title registers (ps3_ui_set_font, ps3_ui_set_prompt_png); the panel stays the
fallback without a font. cellSaveData.c posts the picture's model beside the
panel; its selection, sorting, focus, cancel and overwrite rules are unchanged.
cellPad.c keeps the device last used for the automatic prompt style, and Esc and
Backspace go back while a dialog is open (the window no longer quits on Esc
then). PS3_SAVES_SCREEN_DUMP=<dir> writes each picture (tests).

The dialog presents itself: a title that calls it flips nothing until it
returns, and the overlays were drawn only in presents that follow the title's
flips, so in a windowed native release nothing drew the dialog; after 4 s it
took the title's first entry (a SAVE over that save, whichever was loaded).
The backend now counts its window presents and offers present_again (the last
frame again with the overlays, under the present mutex); the dialog calls it
when no present came for 45 ms.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
